   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Trying something out",
     "texto": [
      "**-아/어 보다** adds the idea of trying an action: 먹다 → **먹어 보다** (to try eating), 입다 → **입어 보다** (to try clothes on), 하다 → **해 보다** (to try doing it). The form combines with tense and speech level: 먹어 **봤어요** (I tried it) and 한번 먹어 **보세요** (please try it once)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Difference from 적이 있어요",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)ㄴ 적이 있어요** talks about an experience you have had; **-아/어 보다** talks about something you try or attempt.",
      "먹은 적이 있어요 = I've eaten it before. 먹어 봤어요 = I've tried it (I tried it)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
